# Launcher catalog, read by the window server (zview): what the right-click
# desktop menu offers -- the fallback launcher that works even with no dock.
# The dock keeps its OWN catalog, /usr/hr/etc/dock: the two lists are
# independent, so an app can sit in this menu without a dock icon (or the
# other way round).
# One line per app:  name:execpath:multi:args   (the last two optional)
#   name        menu label AND the app's title base: by convention it equals
#               the title the program declares in its HRAPP, which is how the
#               menu's single-instance re-raise matches windows to this entry.
#   execpath    program, run from the menu with these arguments
#   multi       1 = may open many copies (menu shows "New <name>...");
#               0 = single instance (a second launch raises it instead)
#   args        extra command-line arguments, blank-separated, passed to the
#               program at launch
#
# The window itself -- title, size, icon while hidden, whether it may be
# stretched -- is NOT configured here: the application declares it at
# start-up (hr_open, see inc/hrapp.h), so a program can also be run straight
# from a shell.
#
# The rc script /usr/hr/etc/rc runs at desktop start-up: it starts the dock,
# and anything else that should be genuinely RESIDENT from power-on.
Shell:/usr/hr/bin/zterm:1
Files:/usr/hr/bin/zfile:1
Editor:/usr/hr/bin/zedit:1
Mail:/usr/hr/bin/zmail:0
Manual:/usr/hr/bin/zman:0
Calculator:/usr/hr/bin/zcalc:0
Printer:/usr/hr/bin/zprint:0
Monitor:/usr/hr/bin/zmon:0
Puzzle:/usr/hr/bin/zpuzzle:0
Maze:/usr/hr/bin/zmaze:0
Clock:/usr/hr/bin/zclock:0
